===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|de|De-Aar.ogg}}
* {{IPA|de|/aːɐ̯/}}
* {{rhymes|de|aːɐ̯|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|ar}}, {{m|gmh|arn}}, from {{inh|de|goh|aro}}, {{m|goh|arn}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*arō}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*arô}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|((<m,es:s>,<m.weak>))}}

# {{lb|de|poetic|formal|or|dated}} [[eagle]]
#: {{syn|de|Adler}}
#* {{quote-book|de|year=1864|author=Franz Pfeiffer|title=Deutsche Classiker des Mittelalters, Erster Band: Walther von der Vogelweide|page=245
|passage=Er habe zwiefache Kaiserstärke: des '''Aares''' Milde und des Löwen Kraft: diesen zweien vermöge nichts zu widerstehen.|t=He has twofold strengths as Kaiser: the '''eagle's''' clemency and the lion's power: nothing should be able to resist these two.}}
#* '''1869''', Ferdinand Freiligrath, ''Pibroch of Donald Dhu'', in his ''Gedichte'', page 315:
#*: {{quote|de|Feder des '''Aaren'''!|Feather of the '''eagle'''!}}
#* '''1808''', {{w|Heinrich von Kleist}} († 1811), ''Die Herrmannschlacht. Ein Drama'', a drama, in: '''1870''', ''H. v. Kleists Werke. Kritisch durchgesehene Ausgabe. Erster Band'', edited by Heinrich Kurz, page 281:
#*: {{quote|de|[...] der Habicht rupft / Die Brut des '''Aars''' [...]|the hawk fleeces / the '''eagle's''' brood}}

=====Declension=====
{{de-ndecl|((<m,es:s>,<m.weak>))}}

===Etymology 2===
Attested as {{der|de|LL.|Arola}}, {{m|la|Arula}} in the 7th century, from a pre-Indo-European hydronym {{m|und|*ar-|t=watercourse}}, also present in several other {{w|Old European hydronymy}} names such as {{m|en|Ahr}} in [[Rhineland]], {{m|en|Ar}} in [[Meurthe-et-Moselle]], {{m|en|l'Arc}} in both [[Savoie]] and [[Bouches-du-Rhône]], {{m|en|Hérault}} ({{cog|oc|Erau}}) in [[Hérault]], {{m|en|Arre}} in [[Gard]], etc.

